{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___, one of your care team doctors. You're here today for your high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy as part of your reinduction treatment for CNS lymphoma. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. I’m feeling okay—no headaches, no nausea. Just ready to get this cycle done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:23:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. We’ll start with some baseline labs and make sure your port is working well. You mentioned last week you had a cough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, just a mild bronchitis. But it’s completely gone now—no fever, no congestion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We delayed your admission a week for that, which was the right call. We don’t want to risk infection during chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:26:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve also been taking the sodium bicarbonate to keep my urine alkaline. Is that still needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. We’ll continue that today to protect your kidneys from the methotrexate. We’ll give it before and after the infusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:28:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the leucovorin? When does that start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We start leucovorin 24 hours after the methotrexate infusion ends. It helps ‘rescue’ your healthy cells from the chemo’s effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:30:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my desmopressin for diabetes insipidus—I’ve been taking it three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:31:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep that going. In the past, IV fluids have caused low sodium when combined with desmopressin, but your levels look stable today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I remember last time they had to adjust it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:33:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. Your labs this morning are looking good—white count and kidney function are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my seizure meds—levetiracetam—I’ve been taking them regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:35:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue that. No seizures recently?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:35:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not since the last episode a few months ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep everything consistent. Now, we’re going to start the methotrexate infusion around noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:37:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long will that take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-08-18 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "About four hours. We give it slowly to reduce side effects. You’ll stay here under observation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-08-18 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting the methotrexate now—19,440 mg, based on your body surface area. This is cycle 23, and your sixth reinduction cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-08-18 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Infusion is going smoothly. Any nausea or headache?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-08-18 14:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel fine. Just a little tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-08-18 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. We’ll keep an eye on you. You also started temozolomide today—240 mg daily for seven days, then seven off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-08-18 14:03:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I took the first dose this morning with ondansetron. No stomach issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-08-18 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Infusion is complete. Great job tolerating it. We’ll continue IV fluids and bicarbonate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-08-19 05:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We drew some labs. Your white count is a bit low at 3.5, but that’s expected. Kidney function is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-08-19 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-08-19 05:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not unusual after chemo. We’ll monitor it. Your sodium is 134—on the lower side but still in range. We’re keeping desmopressin as is."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-08-19 05:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. When will we check the methotrexate level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-08-19 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked it yesterday evening—was 3.3. That’s expected. We’ll check again today and tomorrow to make sure it’s coming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-08-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat methotrexate level is dropping well. We’ve started leucovorin—45 mg every six hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-08-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Any word on my recent MRI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-08-19 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, great news. The MRI shows marked improvement—edema is down and the enhancing lesions have completely resolved. No new areas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-08-19 10:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful to hear. Does that mean the treatment is working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-08-19 10:06:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a very positive sign. There’s still a small area on FLAIR, but no active tumor enhancement. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your latest methotrexate level is 0.12—perfect. That means it’s cleared well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll send you home with leucovorin and bicarbonate to take for one more day. If your level had been higher, we’d keep you longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—everything else stays the same?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Continue your seizure, blood pressure, and depression meds. You’ll follow up in clinic for your next Rituxan in a month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did very well. Stay hydrated, watch for fever or confusion, and call if anything seems off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. And I’ll keep taking the temozolomide as scheduled?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, seven days on, seven off. We’ll review it at your next visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the port—this new one on the left side—is healing well?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the site looks clean and healing. No signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried after the last one opened up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-08-20 06:39:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re keeping a close eye. You’re stable and ready for discharge. Paperwork will be ready soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2186-08-20 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you understand to take leucovorin and bicarbonate for 24 hours at home, then stop?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2186-08-20 20:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, every six hours for one day. Then follow up in clinic next month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2186-08-20 20:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re cleared to go home. Take care, and we’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2186-08-20 20:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’ll be in touch if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2186-08-20 20:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here if you need us. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2186-08-20 20:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. Have a good evening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2186-08-20 20:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2186-08-20 21:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Discharge confirmed. All set."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-08-18 10:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-08-20 21:10:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with recurrent primary central nervous system lymphoma was admitted for his 23rd cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy as part of reinduction therapy. He presented in stable condition after recovering from a recent bronchitis, which delayed admission by one week. He received methotrexate 8 g/m² with urinary alkalinization and started temozolomide 240 mg daily for a 7-day on/7-day off cycle. Leucovorin rescue was initiated 24 hours post-infusion. His methotrexate level declined appropriately to 0.12, and he tolerated treatment well without nausea, seizures, or complications. Sodium remained stable without need for desmopressin adjustment. MRI showed marked improvement with resolution of enhancing lesions and reduced edema. He was discharged home with instructions to continue leucovorin and bicarbonate for 24 hours, resume all home medications, and follow up in clinic for Rituxan and ongoing management.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Hip joint replacement",
      "Personal history of other infectious and parasitic diseases",
      "Personal history of tobacco use",
      "Personal history of tuberculosis",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Unspecified adjustment reaction"
    ]
  }
}
